         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### 13.82 Billion Years — The Universe Today\n\nThis is the universe as we see it today: clusters of galaxies, our own galaxy the Milky Way, and our solar system around an ordinary star.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img src=\"https://www.historytracers.org/images/ESA/Planck_history_of_Universe.jpg\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 2</b>: Planck history of the Universe. ESA - C. Carreau.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
